<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="194" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Children follow an ordinary parent reassigned to another business unit (I-6 drift, #2339)</title>
    <phase>Session 28: UAC (owner round 128, 2026-10-27)</phase>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes record ownership (MDA access) and file containers in a scheduled writer; .cs; access-control.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Extends the Secure-child reconcile engine without weakening its isolation guarantees; adds a relocation purpose for SPE files.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches Services/Access/SecureChild*, RecordOwnershipResolver (read only, unless a defect is found), DocumentContainerRelocator and their tests. No overlap with task 193 or R3's GHSA branch.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, access-control, background, dataverse, spe, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
    <origin>
      GitHub #2339; owner round 128 item 3. The owner said, verbatim: "yes this is a gap that should be closed; also note that e-billing-r1 is asking the same and related questions; i will refer that project to you in order to ensure consistency; this fix should be addressed in this project".
    </origin>
  </metadata>

  <goal>
When an ordinary (non-Secure) matter, project, work assignment or service request moves to another owner team or business unit, every team-owned child filed under it is re-owned within minutes. Each child moves to the owner RecordOwnershipResolver answers (rule I-6), and each re-owned document's file moves to its new business unit's container. Secure-team-owned rows are never touched, and nothing is moved into or out of isolation by this path.
  </goal>

  <component-justification>
    1. Existing: SecureChildReconciler / SecureChildReconciliationJob (Services/Access) already walk a root's descendants and re-own them to a fixpoint through RecordOwnershipResolver. DocumentContainerRelocator already moves a document's file when it is queued in sprk_relocationpending. ReownOrdinaryRowAsync (:495) is an existing conditional (If-Match) ordinary re-own.
    2. Extension: add an ordinary-move mode to the same engine and job, and a new RelocationPurpose. No new job class, no new table, no new column.
    3. Cost of doing nothing: after an MDA reassignment, children stay in the old business unit. Model-driven-app users see the parent and its children by different business units, and files stay in the old business unit's container. Rule I-6 is breached indefinitely.
  </component-justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    1. Trigger. In the job's recent-changes pass, also list ordinary core records (matter, project, work assignment, service request; sprk_issecure not true) whose modifiedon is at or after the watermark. First verify on dev, read-only, that a platform Assign bumps modifiedon on the core record. If it does not, stop and report (escalation trigger).
    2. Decide. For each listed root, walk its descendants with the existing pass (lineage tables, stamps, look-through). For each row OWNED BY A BUSINESS UNIT DEFAULT TEAM, ask RecordOwnershipResolver (ContextFor(row) → ResolveOwnerAsync).
       - The answer is a different ordinary team → plan a move.
       - The row is Secure-team-owned, or the answer is the Secure team, or the answer would release isolation → untouched in this mode (the existing Secure pass owns those).
       - The row is user-owned → untouched and reported (outside-the-product creates stay user-owned, interim accepted under I-6).
       - The resolver refuses → reported, not moved.
       - A child filed under several core records in different business units takes the resolver's own deterministic answer (primary parent first).
    3. Write. Each move is an Assign through the reconciler's existing assign-and-read-back (or ReownOrdinaryRowAsync's If-Match form, widened from its two-table allow-list to the lineage tables), with the previous owner logged first.
       - For a sprk_document whose owning business unit changes, set sprk_relocationpending with a new RelocationPurpose.BusinessUnitMove in the same write.
       - The existing 2-minute settle step relocates its file via DocumentContainerRelocator, capped by MaxRelocationsPerRun.
       - The relocator must refuse a document under a Secure record (never move a Secure file by this purpose).
    4. Switches and caps. A new switch, `SecureChild:Reconciliation:OrdinaryMovesWritesEnabled`, defaults to false: report-only. The report lists planned moves per root (counts, plus samples capped at MaxSampledChanges). Moves are capped per run (reuse MaxRootsPerRun; add MaxOrdinaryMovesPerRun, default 200). A capped or incomplete root is carried to the next run and reported, as the Secure pass does.
    5. Lineage completeness: compare SecureChildLineage.Children with CoreAncestorResolver's child list and the I-6 census. Any child table that the census says is team-owned but that is missing from the walk is either added or listed in the PR as a known limit with a filed issue. The ebilling-r1 invoice-family tables are not on master yet; record in notes/task-194-ordinary-parent-move.md that ebilling adds them to SecureChildLineage / CoreAncestorResolver when it lands them, so they follow by the same mechanism.
    6. Docs: update docs/guides/UAC-ACCESS-MODEL-GUIDE.md §7 (children now follow, within about 2 minutes plus the run) and the DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md I-6 row (L4 owner for ordinary parent moves).
    7. Tests:
       - must-fire: a parent moved from business unit A to B gets its team-owned children re-owned to B's default team, read back, and its document queued and relocated.
       - must-not-fire: Secure-team-owned children, user-owned children, a root whose children already match, and the switch off (report only, no write).
       - never release: an ordinary-mode run never changes a Secure-team-owned row.
       - multi-parent: the resolver's primary-parent answer is applied.
       - Perturbation-check the must-fire tests.
    8. Run the ArchTests (including RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests), the filtered unit tests, and both integration suites in full. Measure the BFF publish delta against a fresh master build. Open a PR; merge with both checks green. Deploy via R3 (owner go). First dev run is report-only. UAC reads the report and the owner gives the go before the switch is set. Then run the server gate.
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    - After the switch is on, an MDA reassignment of an ordinary matter, project or work assignment to another business unit re-owns its team-owned children to the new business unit's default team within 2 minutes plus the run, verified live on dev.
    - The re-owned documents' files are in the new business unit's container (verified live, file count and container id).
    - With the switch off, the run writes nothing and reports the planned moves.
    - No Secure-team-owned row and no Secure file is changed by this mode (test plus the live census unchanged).
    - User-owned children are reported, not moved.
    - Negative: no new job class, no plugin, no change to the Secure pass's behaviour (existing SecureChild* tests unchanged).
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A platform Assign does not bump the core record's modifiedon, so the recent-changes pass cannot see the move without a different detection design.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <constraints>
    - CLAUDE.md §9-§11, §10 (publish delta); ADR-002 (no plugins); ADR-036/052 (scheduled work stays in the existing IScheduledJob); I-2 and I-6 (DATAVERSE-WRITE-PATH-ARCHITECTURE.md).
    - Never release a row from isolation; never touch a Secure-team-owned row in ordinary mode.
    - Never purge or delete SPE containers. The relocator moves files only.
    - Writes default off; turning them on in an environment needs the owner's go after UAC reads the report-only run.
  </constraints>
</task>
